reason=APPLY FIX IN EDARSAHUB_DESARROLLO / PREVIEW ONLY. Two coupled defects are confirmed. (1) Reportes ISCAM UI/runtime is stale/incomplete even though canonical Comercial V2 already contains closed-day data. SQL Auditor Issue #77 proved ESTELAR has fecha_operacion=2026-09-06 while the Reportes ISCAM screen showed only through 2026-09-05. The canonical automatic scheduler sync_comercial_v2 is active and processing 5/5 units. Fix ISCAM so Ventas por Periodo reads/refetches the exact same canonical contract as Dashboard Ejecutivo (KPIsCanonicosService.resumen_periodo_desglosado / canonical Comercial V2), respecting SoftRestaurant operational date by turnos.apertura and cierre IS NOT NULL only as eligibility. Do not use Sync_Sales or report-specific POS SQL. First reproduce in preview for ESTELAR September 2026 and compare endpoint output against the Executive canonical result; identify whether the stale result is backend route/query, cache, frontend load/refetch, or deployment mismatch and correct the actual cause. Add an ISCAM freshness/status contract (reuse existing canonical scheduler/resync/status services where possible) that exposes expected latest CLOSED operational date, latest canonical available date, missing closed dates, and stale boolean for selected unit/range. In ReportesISCAMPage.jsx show compact status such as 'Actualizado hasta DD/MM/YYYY'. When stale/missing closed dates exist, show a compact 'Sincronizar faltantes' button beside Excel/PDF with RefreshCw/spinner, disabled while running, success/error feedback, and automatic refetch of both status and report. Manual action must use existing canonical RBAC-protected Comercial V2 resync handler, DRY RUN first then REAL only if dry-run succeeds, safely chunk large ranges, and verify canonical freshness after completion. Never call or re-enable legacy inteligencia_comercial_sync, Sistema_SyncPOS_Config, or Sync_Sales. Current open day must not be treated as a missing closed day. Acceptance: ESTELAR day 2026-09-06 appears in ISCAM Ventas por Periodo and equals Dashboard Ejecutivo canonical values; if all closed dates are present button is hidden/disabled as appropriate; if a closed date is missing button appears and canonical resync path is invoked; frontend refreshes immediately after success. (2) Fix false failure classification in dbo.Scheduler_BitacoraJobs for sync_comercial_v2. SQL Auditor Issue #78 showed a FINISH with DetallesJSON status='completado', units 5/5, failed_count=0, error_detail=null, but Exito=0. Current development code has _normalize_comercial_sync_status mapping COMPLETADO to success, so determine whether runtime is stale or another path still writes raw Spanish status. Make classification robust at the canonical logging boundary so success/completed/completado/OK-equivalent successful terminal states persist Exito=1 without changing genuine partial/failed semantics. Add regression tests proving status COMPLETADO yields Exito=1 and that FAILED/PARCIAL are not misclassified. Validate one preview execution/log after deployment: START and FINISH, Exito=1, no error for a 5/5 successful Comercial V2 run. Run targeted backend tests and frontend tests/build. Return evidence: root cause, changed files, tests, commit SHA, preview runtime/deploy SHA, exact ISCAM ESTELAR 2026-09-06 comparison, and Scheduler_BitacoraJobs validation. Do not touch Production.